# =============================================================================
# token_budget.env — operator-tunable pacing/tiering of the Claude layer.
#
# Copy to ~/recon/state/token_budget.env and `recon-restart` to apply. The
# daemon sources it BEFORE every interval/model default, so these values win.
# Absent => stock defaults. Fully reversible: delete the file + restart. NOT
# git-mirrored (lives under ~/recon/state, machine-local).
#
# PROFILE: "economic but don't hurt ourselves". The philosophy is CUT WASTE,
# KEEP MUSCLE:
#   - Downtier DISCRIMINATIVE calls (judging/triage) to cheaper models — near-
#     zero quality loss.  Keep CREATIVE calls (hypothesis generation) on Opus.
#   - Pace BULK lanes hard (they have long TTLs; hourly was overkill).
#   - Keep the FINDING ENGINE (hunter) responsive to fresh surface — that's the
#     edge. Trim its cost via model-tiering, NOT by starving its cadence.
#   - DO NOT cheap out on the VERIFY precision gate: it fires only on confirmed
#     findings (rare, so it costs little) and it's what keeps reports from being
#     overclaimed/closed-N/A. It also backstops the hunter, so hunter
#     adjudication can safely run on Sonnet. => VERIFY stays fully on Opus.
# =============================================================================

# ---- ai-hunter (dominant spender: Opus x2 per target) -----------------------
# stock: 1800 (30m). Kept RESPONSIVE (60m, not 90m+) — racing fresh endpoints is
# the edge. Cost is trimmed by tiering adjudication below, not by starving it.
AI_HUNTER_INTERVAL=3600            # 60m
# Adjudication (judging real probe responses vs expected) is discriminative, not
# creative — Sonnet does it well, and any "confirmed" it mints still passes the
# Opus VERIFY panel before #review. Keep HUNTER_MODEL=opus for the creative
# hypothesis step (the actual value).  stock: opus (inherits HUNTER_MODEL).
HUNTER_ADJ_MODEL=sonnet

# ---- ai-analyze (bulk triage; haiku + sonnet on high score) -----------------
# stock: 3600 (1h). 14d re-analyse TTL => hourly is pure waste. Pure economy.
AI_ANALYZE_INTERVAL=10800         # 3h
# stock: 60. Slightly higher => fewer sonnet escalations; high-value still gets
# sonnet. 70 is a gentle middle (not 75) so mid-tier assets keep the good model.
ANALYZE_HI_SCORE=70

# ---- ai-vision (screenshot triage; haiku, cheap) ----------------------------
# stock: 3600 (1h). 21d TTL; drains fast; haiku. Pure economy, no muscle here.
AI_VISION_INTERVAL=14400          # 4h

# ---- standing research routines ---------------------------------------------
# stock: 86400 (daily) vulns. Research is "the edge" — trim gently (2 days, not
# 3+). tooling/kb/detect stay weekly (unchanged). CVE/KEV DATA feeds still run
# hourly/daily; this is only the Claude synthesis layer.
RESEARCH_VULNS_INTERVAL=172800    # every 2 days

# ---- VERIFY (FP-kill precision gate) — DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED ----------------
# Left on stock (CONSENSUS_MODEL/CLAUDE_ESCALATE_MODEL = opus). Fires only on
# confirmed findings, so it's low-volume + high-value: cheap to keep, costly to
# weaken. This is the "don't hurt ourselves" line.

# ---- (optional, HARDER economy — only if you must squeeze more) --------------
# Uncomment to go further; each trades some capability for tokens.
# AI_HUNTER_INTERVAL=5400         # 90m hunter (fewer fresh targets/day)
# CONSENSUS_MODEL=sonnet          # cheaper FP-panel (risks report precision)
# CLAUDE_ESCALATE_MODEL=sonnet    # VERIFY never escalates to Opus
# RESEARCH_VULNS_INTERVAL=259200  # research every 3 days
